IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-seat`

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore): worked cases for the seat layer (eca-seat).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Act before any run; the comment beside each assertion says which words decide it.
-- Amounts, fees, limits and periods in these cases are test figures: the Act states none of them.
-- Each case ends with an assertion; the number written equal to the number satisfied is printed by check.sh.


-- ======================================================================
-- Ms Lim, a cashier, was dismissed without notice on 31 August 2025 and is owed salary; the cases below follow her questions in the Act's order
-- ======================================================================

-- s 3(1): a claim for a specified employment dispute needs a mediation request first; no tripartite mediation was conducted
#ASSERT `Must I submit a mediation request first` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(8): "This section does not apply to a claim if a tripartite mediation has been conducted"
#ASSERT `Must I submit a mediation request first` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3(1) speaks of a claim lodged for a specified employment dispute; a claim for none is not spoken to
#ASSERT `Must I submit a mediation request first` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(2)(f): not later than 6 months after the last day of employment, 31 August 2025; February 2026 has 28 days (fork F6)
#ASSERT `By what date must I submit my request` `Another specified employment dispute` TRUE 31 8 2025 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- s 3(2)(d): not later than one month after the date of the dismissal
#ASSERT `By what date must I submit my request` `Wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968` TRUE 15 1 2026 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2026)
-- s 3(2)(g): not later than one year after the date the material facts occurred (employment not ended)
#ASSERT `By what date must I submit my request` `Another specified employment dispute` FALSE 15 6 2025 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2026)
-- s 3(2)(f) counts from the last day of employment and the date is not known
#ASSERT `By what date must I submit my request` `Another specified employment dispute` TRUE 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(2): submitted on the last day, 28 February 2026, is by the time
#ASSERT `Is my request in time` `Another specified employment dispute` TRUE 31 8 2025 28 2 2026 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(2): a day after the last day is not by the time ("must be submitted ... by the following time")
#ASSERT `Is my request in time` `Another specified employment dispute` TRUE 31 8 2025 1 3 2026 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the last day cannot be worked out without the date it counts from
#ASSERT `Is my request in time` `Another specified employment dispute` TRUE 0 0 0 1 3 2026 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(3)(a): no claim for an amount, so (i) is met; the material facts were not earlier than one year before the request (exactly one year); not listed before
#ASSERT `Must my request list this dispute` FALSE FALSE 1 6 2025 1 6 2026 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(3)(a)(ii): the material facts occurred one year and a day before the request; "not earlier than one year before" is a period in the text's own words, so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (a))
#ASSERT `Must my request list this dispute` FALSE FALSE 31 5 2025 1 6 2026 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3(3)(c): a claim for an amount exists and section 16 bars lodging it
#ASSERT `Must my request leave this dispute out` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(3)(c): "must not list ... if" both hold; section 16 does not bar it
#ASSERT `Must my request leave this dispute out` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3(3)(d): accompanied by the prescribed fee; the fee paid equals the prescribed fee (test figure)
#ASSERT `Is my mediation fee enough` 50 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(3)(d): less than the prescribed fee
#ASSERT `Is my mediation fee enough` 49 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the prescribed fee is in regulations that are not among the sources, and 0 means not known
#ASSERT `Is my mediation fee enough` 50 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(4)(a)(i): the request does not comply with s 3(2) and (3)
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner refuse my request` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(4)(a): refusal is "if" (i) or (ii); neither holds
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner refuse my request` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3(4)(b): the Commissioner may waive, remit or refund the fee, wholly or in part, with no condition
#ASSERT `May my mediation fee be waived` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(5): upon accepting the request, the Commissioner must refer every listed dispute
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner refer my dispute to a mediator` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(5) arises "Upon accepting the mediation request"; not yet accepted, and "upon" is read as "where" (assumed, not ruled, fork F9)
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner refer my dispute to a mediator` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(1): after the dispute is referred, the approved mediator must conduct the first session
#ASSERT `Must the mediator hold the first session` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(1) is for a dispute "referred" to the mediator, "after that dispute is referred"; read as "where" (assumed, not ruled, fork F9)
#ASSERT `Must the mediator hold the first session` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(2): need not conduct any session if satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement
#ASSERT `May the mediator decide not to hold a session` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(2): "need not ... if satisfied"; the mediator is not satisfied
#ASSERT `May the mediator decide not to hold a session` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(3): each mediation session must be held in private
#ASSERT `Is my mediation session private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(3) speaks of "Each mediation session" under this Part
#ASSERT `Is my mediation session private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(5)(a) with s 4(4): two or more claimants, same respondent, similar disputes
#ASSERT `May the same mediator take my dispute with others` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(5): "Subsection (4) applies where" one of three cases arises, and none does (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `May the same mediator take my dispute with others` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(1)(b): a party "cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor"
#ASSERT `Can this person represent a party at the mediation` `An individual` `An advocate and solicitor` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(2)(b): a body corporate may be represented by a full-time employee
#ASSERT `Can this person represent a party at the mediation` `A body corporate` `A full-time employee of the party` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 5(3): whether regulations prescribe the individual is outside the sources
#ASSERT `Can this person represent a party at the mediation` `An individual` `Another individual prescribed by regulations` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(4): not settled and not withdrawn
#ASSERT `Is my dispute unresolved` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(4): a settled dispute is not unresolved
#ASSERT `Is my dispute unresolved` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(2)(a): the respondent, given reasonable notice, does not attend
#ASSERT `Must the mediator give me a certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(2): issue "if" (a), (b) or (c); none holds
#ASSERT `Must the mediator give me a certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(2) is for an "unresolved" dispute; this one is settled
#ASSERT `Must the mediator give me a certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(1): "This section applies where" a request is submitted and a dispute referred; no request was submitted, so section 6 does not apply (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Must the mediator give me a certificate` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(3): a claimant who, without reasonable excuse, fails to attend any session
#ASSERT `Can the mediator refuse me a certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(3): the claimant did not fail to attend
#ASSERT `Can the mediator refuse me a certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(1)(a): in the form prescribed by Rules of Court (the person says it is)
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement in the prescribed form` TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(a): "must enter into a settlement agreement in the form prescribed"
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement in the prescribed form` TRUE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the form is in Rules of Court that are not among the sources
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement in the prescribed form` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(1) begins "Where a specified employment dispute is settled"; nothing is settled (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement in the prescribed form` FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(1)(b): must not exceed the limit; equal is within (test figures)
#ASSERT `Is my settlement within the claim limit for salary-type disputes` TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(b): "must not exceed the prescribed claim limit"
#ASSERT `Is my settlement within the claim limit for salary-type disputes` TRUE 101 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the limit is prescribed under section 12(8)(e); 0 means not known
#ASSERT `Is my settlement within the claim limit for salary-type disputes` TRUE 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(1)(c): must not exceed the limit; equal is within
#ASSERT `Is my settlement within the claim limit for wrongful dismissal` TRUE 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(c): "must not exceed the prescribed claim limit"
#ASSERT `Is my settlement within the claim limit for wrongful dismissal` TRUE 101 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(1)(d): signed by or on behalf of each party
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement signed by or for every party` TRUE 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(d): "must be signed by or on behalf of each party"
#ASSERT `Is my settlement agreement signed by or for every party` TRUE 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(2): on the application of any party to it
#ASSERT `May a District Court register my settlement agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(2): the power is "on the application of any party"; no party applied, and "on" is read as "where" (assumed, not ruled, fork F9)
#ASSERT `May a District Court register my settlement agreement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(2): may refuse if the application is not made within the prescribed period
#ASSERT `May a District Court refuse because the application is late` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(2): "may refuse ... if" late; it was in time
#ASSERT `May a District Court refuse because the application is late` Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the period is in Rules of Court that are not among the sources
#ASSERT `May a District Court refuse because the application is late` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(3)(a): a judgment "entered on the date of registration"
#ASSERT `From what date does my registered agreement have the force of a judgment` TRUE 5 5 2026 EQUALS JUST (Date 5 5 2026)
-- s 7(3) is for an agreement "registered in a District Court"
#ASSERT `From what date does my registered agreement have the force of a judgment` FALSE 5 5 2026 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(3)(b): proceedings may be taken on it as on a judgment of a District Court
#ASSERT `Can I take proceedings on my registered agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(3)(b) begins "Where the settlement agreement is registered"; it is not (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Can I take proceedings on my registered agreement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(3)(c): carries interest as a judgment debt
#ASSERT `Does my registered amount carry interest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(3)(c) begins "Where the settlement agreement is registered"; it is not (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Does my registered amount carry interest` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(4): a party may apply within the prescribed period
#ASSERT `May I apply to set aside the registration` TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(4) gives the permission "within the period prescribed" by Rules of Court; outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (ruled 2026-11-05, (a); the period is fixed by reference, fork F10)
#ASSERT `May I apply to set aside the registration` TRUE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(4) begins "Where a settlement agreement is registered in a District Court"; it is not (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `May I apply to set aside the registration` FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(6)(a) satisfied, so s 7(5)(b)(i) allows the court to set the agreement aside
#ASSERT `Can a District Court set aside my settlement agreement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(5): "if any condition in subsection (6) is satisfied"; none is
#ASSERT `Can a District Court set aside my settlement agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(2)(a): by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer
#ASSERT `Is my claim made by and against the right people` `The employee` `The employer of the employee` Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(2)(b): against a person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968
#ASSERT `Is my claim made by and against the right people` `The employee` `A person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 for the employee's salary` Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(2): "The claim must be made" by an employee who is prescribed or in a prescribed class; the employee is not
#ASSERT `Is my claim made by and against the right people` `The employee` `The employer of the employee` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- which employees are prescribed is in regulations that are not among the sources
#ASSERT `Is my claim made by and against the right people` `The employee` `The employer of the employee` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(3)(a): amounts alleged to be payable
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(3)(b): reinstatement in a wrongful dismissal case
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(3): for amounts, or reinstatement in a wrongful dismissal case; neither
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(3): "either or both": amounts, and reinstatement outside a wrongful dismissal case, which only adds nothing
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(3)(a): amounts alleged to be payable, in a wrongful dismissal case
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(3): both limbs
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(3): a wrongful dismissal claim for neither amounts nor reinstatement
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(3): for neither (no combination of these three yes-or-no facts gives NOTHING: the question is open, see NOTES, Open questions)
#ASSERT `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(4): each amount must relate to a specified employment dispute
#ASSERT `Does each amount relate to a specified employment dispute` 3 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(4): one amount does not
#ASSERT `Does each amount relate to a specified employment dispute` 3 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(5): a certificate for every specified employment dispute
#ASSERT `Is my claim supported by a certificate for every dispute` 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(5): one dispute has no certificate
#ASSERT `Is my claim supported by a certificate for every dispute` 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(6): within the prescribed period (60 days, a test figure) after the date of issue; 1 January + 60 days is 2 March
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my claim` 1 1 2026 2 3 2026 60 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(6): one day after the 60th day
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my claim` 1 1 2026 3 3 2026 60 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the prescribed period is in regulations that are not among the sources
#ASSERT `Am I in time to lodge my claim` 1 1 2026 2 3 2026 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12(7)(a): must not exceed the limit; equal is within (test figures)
#ASSERT `Is the total I claim within the claim limits` 20000 20000 0 20000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(7)(a): "must not exceed the prescribed claim limit"
#ASSERT `Is the total I claim within the claim limits` 20001 20000 0 20000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- one limit is not known, so the conditions cannot be said to be satisfied
#ASSERT `Is the total I claim within the claim limits` 20000 0 0 20000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15(1)(a): the total exceeds the limit
#ASSERT `May I abandon the excess` 20001 20000 0 20000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(1) begins "Where" a total exceeds its limit; neither does (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `May I abandon the excess` 20000 20000 0 20000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(2)(b): if the claimant abandons the excess, the tribunal has jurisdiction
#ASSERT `If I abandon the excess, may the tribunal hear my claim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(2): "If the claimant abandons the excess amount"; the claimant does not
#ASSERT `If I abandon the excess, may the tribunal hear my claim` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(2)(c)
#ASSERT `If I abandon the excess, does the order discharge all demands` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(2): "If the claimant abandons the excess amount"; the claimant does not
#ASSERT `If I abandon the excess, does the order discharge all demands` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(3): cannot recover the excess in a tribunal or any other court
#ASSERT `Can I not recover the amount I abandoned` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(3): "Where the claimant has abandoned the excess amount"; the claimant has not (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Can I not recover the amount I abandoned` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14: cannot be divided if the only reason is to bring each part within the jurisdiction
#ASSERT `Is splitting my claim barred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 14 bars division "if the only reason" is to bring each total within the jurisdiction; the reason is another one (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `Is splitting my claim barred` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(1)(a): proceedings pending in another court
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred by other proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(1)(b): the Commissioner decided the dispute under section 115
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred by other proceedings` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(1) bars lodging "if" (a) or (b); neither holds (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred by other proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(2): once lodged, no proceedings in any other court
#ASSERT `Is starting other proceedings barred after I lodge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(2): "unless the claim is withdrawn, discontinued or dismissed for lack of jurisdiction"
#ASSERT `Is starting other proceedings barred after I lodge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(2): "where a claim ... is lodged with a tribunal"; none is (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Is starting other proceedings barred after I lodge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(3): dismissed; salary in lieu of notice (First Schedule item 17); representations under s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 not withdrawn
#ASSERT `Am I barred from lodging after making representations` TRUE TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(3)(a): the bar is "if" written representations were made under s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 or s 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993; none were (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `Am I barred from lodging after making representations` TRUE TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `No such representations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(4)(a)(i): the employee makes representations under s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960
#ASSERT `Is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(4)(a): deemed discontinued "if the employee makes representations"; none made
#ASSERT `Is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `No such representations` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(4): "Where an employee is dismissed, and ... lodges ... a claim"; not so (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` FALSE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(4)(b): with effect from the date the employee makes the representations
#ASSERT `From what date is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` 7 7 2026 EQUALS JUST (Date 7 7 2026)
-- s 16(4)(b) follows from (a), which does not apply
#ASSERT `From what date is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` TRUE (`A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`) `No such representations` 7 7 2026 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 16(5): dismissed; representations under s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 not withdrawn
#ASSERT `Am I barred from a wrongful dismissal claim after making representations` TRUE TRUE `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(5)(a) names only s 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960: "if" the representations are not those, the bar does not arise (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `Am I barred from a wrongful dismissal claim after making representations` TRUE TRUE `Representations in writing under section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(6)(a): deemed discontinued if the employee makes representations under s 35(3)
#ASSERT `Is my lodged wrongful dismissal claim deemed discontinued` TRUE `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(6)(a): "if the employee makes representations"; none made
#ASSERT `Is my lodged wrongful dismissal claim deemed discontinued` TRUE `No such representations` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(7): made s 8B(1) representations; the Minister has not allowed a mediation request and no certificate
#ASSERT `Am I barred from claiming employment assistance payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(7): "unless" (a) the Minister allows and (b) a certificate is issued; both
#ASSERT `Am I barred from claiming employment assistance payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(7): "Where an employee has made representations"; none made (ruled 2026-11-05, (b))
#ASSERT `Am I barred from claiming employment assistance payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(8)(a): stayed until the Minister decides
#ASSERT `Is my employment assistance payment claim stayed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(8)(a): "until that Minister decides"; the Minister has decided
#ASSERT `Is my employment assistance payment claim stayed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(8)(c): the Minister decides to allow
#ASSERT `May I proceed with my employment assistance payment claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(8)(c) and (b): the Minister decided not to allow, so the claim is deemed discontinued
#ASSERT `May I proceed with my employment assistance payment claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(8)(c): "if that Minister decides to allow"; no decision yet, so the claim is still stayed under (a) (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `May I proceed with my employment assistance payment claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(9): the employer did not raise the ground during the Part 2 mediation
#ASSERT `Is my employer barred from the eligibility defence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 16(9) bars the defence "if the employer did not raise" it; the employer did (the "if" rule of 2026-10-29)
#ASSERT `Is my employer barred from the eligibility defence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(1): all of s 12(2) to (7) satisfied
#ASSERT `Does the tribunal have jurisdiction over my claim` Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(1) subject to s 15(2)(a): the excess was abandoned, so 12(7) is deemed satisfied
#ASSERT `Does the tribunal have jurisdiction over my claim` Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes No TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 12(1) grants jurisdiction for a claim meeting all requirements; when one fails the text does not say in so many words that there is no jurisdiction (marginal reading (b)); the failing requirement is answered by the s 12(7) question
#ASSERT `Does the tribunal have jurisdiction over my claim` Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes No FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(1): lodged by filing the claim with the Registry
#ASSERT `Is my claim lodged` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 13(1) does not say another way is not a lodging
#ASSERT `Is my claim lodged` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(2)(a)(i): the form and manner prescribed by Rules of Court
#ASSERT `Did I file in the form and manner required` Yes No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 13(2)(a): "Every claim must be filed in the form and manner" of (i) or (ii)
#ASSERT `Did I file in the form and manner required` No No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Rules of Court are not among the sources
#ASSERT `Did I file in the form and manner required` `I am not sure` No EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(2)(b)(i): accompanied by a certificate for every dispute
#ASSERT `Does a certificate for every dispute come with my claim` 2 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 13(2)(b)(i)
#ASSERT `Does a certificate for every dispute come with my claim` 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 13(2)(b)(ii)
#ASSERT `Do the other required documents come with my claim` Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 13(2)(b)(ii): "must be accompanied by any other documents"
#ASSERT `Do the other required documents come with my claim` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- which documents are required is in Rules of Court and practice directions outside the sources
#ASSERT `Do the other required documents come with my claim` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(2)(b)(iii): accompanied by the court fee prescribed (test figure)
#ASSERT `Is my court fee enough` 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 13(2)(b)(iii)
#ASSERT `Is my court fee enough` 99 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the court fee is in Rules of Court that are not among the sources; 0 means not known
#ASSERT `Is my court fee enough` 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(1)(c): a party "cannot be represented by an agent, whether paid or otherwise"
#ASSERT `Can this person represent a party at the tribunal` `An individual` `An agent, whether paid or otherwise` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(2)(a): the Government may be represented by a public officer
#ASSERT `Can this person represent a party at the tribunal` `The Government` `A public officer` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18(1): all proceedings before a tribunal are conducted in private
#ASSERT `Are the proceedings on my claim private` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18(1) speaks of "all proceedings before a tribunal"
#ASSERT `Are the proceedings on my claim private` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18(4)(a) or (b): a prescribed individual or one in a prescribed class
#ASSERT `May the tribunal let this person observe` Yes FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18(4)(c): any other individual the tribunal deems fit
#ASSERT `May the tribunal let this person observe` No TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 18(4): none of the three kinds
#ASSERT `May the tribunal let this person observe` No FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(8): a party without reasonable excuse fails to attend; the tribunal may hear the claim and decide in that party's absence
#ASSERT `May the tribunal decide in my absence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 20(8) is for a party who "without reasonable excuse, fails to attend" (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `May the tribunal decide in my absence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 20(7)(a)
#ASSERT `Must the tribunal have regard to the wrongful dismissal guidelines` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 20(7): "When deciding any claim involving a wrongful dismissal dispute"; "when" is read as "where" (assumed, not ruled, fork F9)
#ASSERT `Must the tribunal have regard to the wrongful dismissal guidelines` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(2): failure to comply with an obligation under a written law specified in the Fourth Schedule (item 1)
#ASSERT `May the tribunal draw an inference from the failure` (`A Fourth Schedule obligation` `Item 1: an employer's obligations under EA 1968 s 95, 95A and 96`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(2) is for obligations under the written laws in the Fourth Schedule
#ASSERT `May the tribunal draw an inference from the failure` `Some other obligation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(3): evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation
#ASSERT `Need my evidence be on oath` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(3): "Subject to subsection (4)": the tribunal requires it
#ASSERT `Need my evidence be on oath` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(6): all evidence and information obtained under (5) must be disclosed to every party
#ASSERT `Must the tribunal disclose what it found` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(6) is for what the tribunal obtained under subsection (5)
#ASSERT `Must the tribunal disclose what it found` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(1)(a)
#ASSERT `Does the person who alleges it bear the burden` TRUE `That the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 27(1) places the burden for the allegations it names
